      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Annotate a class with "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@Suite"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " to have it marked as a test suite on the JUnit Platform. As seen in the following example, selector and filter annotations can be used to control the contents of the suite."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "import org.junit.platform.suite.api.IncludeClassNamePatterns;\nimport org.junit.platform.suite.api.SelectPackages;\nimport org.junit.platform.suite.api.Suite;\nimport org.junit.platform.suite.api.SuiteDisplayName;\n\n@Suite\n@SuiteDisplayName(\"JUnit Platform Suite Demo\")\n@SelectPackages(\"example\")\n@IncludeClassNamePatterns(\".*Tests\")\nclass SuiteDemo {\n}"
              }
            ],
            "language": "java",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "admonition",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "There are numerous configuration options for discovering and filtering tests in a test suite. Please consult the Javadoc of the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "org.junit.platform.suite.api"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "xref",
                    "target": "attachment$api/org.junit.platform.suite.api/org/junit/platform/suite/api/package-summary.html"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " package for a full list of supported annotations and further details."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Additional Configuration Options"
              }
            ],
            "type": "note"
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "example",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "@Suite Example"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@BeforeSuite"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " and "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@AfterSuite"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " annotations can be used on methods inside a "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@Suite"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "-annotated class. They will be executed before and after all tests of the test suite, respectively."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@Suite\n@SelectPackages(\"example\")\nclass BeforeAndAfterSuiteDemo {\n\n\t@BeforeSuite\n\tstatic void beforeSuite() {\n\t\t// executes before the test suite\n\t}\n\n\t@AfterSuite\n\tstatic void afterSuite() {\n\t\t// executes after the test suite\n\t}\n\n}"
              }
            ],
            "language": "java",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "_beforesuite_and_aftersuite",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "@BeforeSuite and @AfterSuite"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Depending on the declared selectors, different suites may contain the same tests, potentially with different configurations. Moreover, tests in a suite are executed in addition to the tests executed by every other test engine, which can result in the same tests being executed twice."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "alt": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "junit platform suite engine duplicate test execution diagram"
              }
            ],
            "attributes": {},
            "caption": null,
            "context": "image",
            "id": null,
            "roles": [
              "text-center"
            ],
            "src": "junit-platform-suite-engine-duplicate-test-execution-diagram.svg",
            "svg": null,
            "target": "junit-platform-suite-engine-duplicate-test-execution-diagram.svg",
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "To prevent duplicate execution of tests within a suite, configure your build tool to include only the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "junit-platform-suite"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " engine, or use a custom naming pattern. For example, name all suites "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "*Suite"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " and all tests "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "*Test"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", and configure your build tool to include only the former."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Alternatively, consider "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "using tags"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "running-tests/tags.html"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " to select specific groups of tests."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
